- **Sister Project LLM Space:** Companion developer workbench for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.
- Available at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow under the MIT license.', 'auto', NULL, 'ok', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_df_a2_intro', 'out_df_paper', '1 Introduction', NULL, 1, 'section', 'The evolution of foundation models has enabled agentic workflows capable of writing code, performing web research, and operating external computational tools. However, deploying agents in production environments exposes severe structural vulnerabilities: unbounded execution risks, context window exhaustion, cascading hallucination loops, and lack of persistent memory across sessions.\\n\\nTo resolve these challenges, DeerFlow 2.0 provides a modular super-agent harness designed for enterprise-grade safety and efficiency. We decouple the lead agent''s reasoning loop from tool execution through a pluggable sandbox layer supporting local container engines and Kubernetes provisioners. Furthermore, we establish a formal delegation contract where subagents inherit execution namespaces without contaminating the parent run state.', 'auto', NULL, 'ok', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_df_a3_arch', 'out_df_paper', '2 System Architecture & Harness Pipeline', NULL, 2, 'section-figure', 'The DeerFlow system topology comprises four coordinated layers: (i) an Nginx reverse-proxy ingress managing persistent Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming connections; (ii) a FastAPI Gateway hosting the embedded LangGraph runtime, authentication, and session routers; (iii) the LangGraph Lead Agent orchestrating a bounded middleware chain including dynamic authorization, session goals, and manual context compaction; and (iv) an isolated Sandbox Provisioner executing shell commands, file modifications, and web crawlers.\\n\\nSubagent delegation is decoupled through a two-tier identifier mechanism: server-side execution keys manage process lifecycles and cancellation fencing, while client tool IDs maintain transparent streaming message tuples.', 'single', NULL, 'ok', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true}', '[{"id":"fig_df_arch_paper","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology and isolated multi-agent orchestration."}]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_df_a1_abs', 'out_df_paper', 'Abstract', NULL, 0, 'section', 'Autonomous language model agents must reliably execute arbitrary software tools, navigate expansive code repositories, synthesize verified solutions, and maintain state over extended operational horizons. We introduce DeerFlow 2.0, an open-source super-agent harness built atop a LangGraph foundation that couples sandboxed execution, hierarchical memory, subagent delegation, and extensible skill protocols. Unlike fragile single-loop architectures, DeerFlow isolates untrusted execution environments within micro-containers, enforces bounded context compaction, and orchestrates delegated subagents with independent namespaces and deterministic lifecycle accounting. On real-world multi-step engineering and research benchmarks, DeerFlow achieves a 78.4% success rate while reducing redundant context tokens by 45% compared to monolithic agent loops.', 'auto', NULL, 'ok', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_df_s1_title', 'out_df_slides', 'Title Slide', NULL, 0, 'title-slide', 'DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness\\n\\nOrchestrating Sub-Agents, Sandboxes, Memory, and Extensible Skills\\n\\nByteDance Open Source & Community Contributors\\nOpen Source AI Symposium 2026', 'auto', NULL, 'ok', NULL, 'Introduce DeerFlow as the #1 trending open-source super-agent framework that transitioned from pure deep research to a universal harness.', '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_df_a4_eval', 'out_df_paper', '3 Experimental Evaluation', NULL, 3, 'section-table', 'We benchmark DeerFlow against baseline agent architectures on multi-step software engineering and complex reasoning tasks. All models were evaluated under identical budget constraints using DeepSeek v3 and Doubao-Seed-2.0 backends.', 'auto', NULL, 'ok', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[["Framework Architecture","Success Rate (%)","Token Cost Ratio","Mean Latency (s)"],["Direct Zero-Shot Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","4.2s"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.40x","38.5s"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.10x","65.2s"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Full Harness)","78.4%","1.70x","24.8s"]],"caption":"Table 1: Task resolution success rate and efficiency metrics.","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_af_c2_ipa', 'out_alphafold_poster', 'Invariant Point Attention (IPA) Module', 2, 1, 'bullets', '- **3D Rigid Body Residue Frames:** Predicts Euclidean rotations and translations $(R_i, \\vec{t}_i) \\in \\text{SE}(3)$ for all amino acid backbones independently.
- **Coordinate Independence:** Mathematical guarantee that computed attention weights remain strictly invariant to global rigid-body rotations and translations in 3D Euclidean space.
- **Torsion Angle Predictions:** Predicts 7 backbone and side-chain dihedral angles per residue $(\\phi, \\psi, \\omega, \\chi_1, \\chi_2, \\chi_3, \\chi_4)$ from local reference frames.
- **Iterative Refinement:** Structural module recycles backbones through 8 shared structural update iterations with stop-gradient propagation.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_af_c2_loss', 'out_alphafold_poster', 'Clamped FAPE Loss & Stereochemistry', 2, 2, 'bullets', '- **Frame Aligned Point Error (FAPE):** Structural loss comparing local residue coordinates across ground-truth frames:

$$\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{FAPE}} = \\frac{1}{N^2} \\sum_{i,j} \\min\\left(d_{\\text{clamp}}, \\|\\vec{x}_{ij}^{\\text{pred}} - \\vec{x}_{ij}^{\\text{true}}\\|\\right)$$

- **Stereochemical Regularization:** Penalizes peptide bond length deviations and van der Waals steric overlap clashes without physical molecular dynamics simulations.
- **pLDDT Confidence:** Predicts local distance difference test score per residue to estimate uncertainty.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_af_c3_benchmark', 'out_alphafold_poster', 'CASP14 Blind Assessment Accuracy', 3, 0, 'bullets-image', '**Dominance Across Free-Modeling & Template Targets:**
- **Free-Modeling (FM):** Achieves GDT_TS of 87.0 on hard free-modeling targets lacking homologous structures in PDB.
- **Side-Chain Fidelity:** Highly accurate placement of rotamer conformations aligns with experimental electron density maps.
- **Global Topology Resolution:** Accurately resolves complex all-beta sheet architectures and knots without human intervention.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[{"id":"fig_casp14","url":"/api/workspaces/alphafold-protein-folding/assets/fig_casp14_benchmark.png","caption":"Figure 2: CASP14 blind assessment median GDT scores across target domains."}]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c1_intro', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Abstract & Physics Motivation', 1, 0, 'bullets', 'Two-particle Bose-Einstein correlations (BEC) of like-sign charged hadrons provide a direct space-time probe of the particle-emitting source in high-energy particle collisions.

- **Quantum Interference:** Identical bosons exhibit constructive wave-function symmetrization, enhancing pairs emitted with small relative momentum ($Q \\to 0$).
- **Space-Time Geometry:** The correlation function directly maps the spatial Fourier transform of the hadronization freeze-out region.
- **LHC Run 2 at 13 TeV:** Highest proton-proton collision energy offers unprecedented access to ultra-high charged-particle multiplicities ($N_{\\text{ch}} \\ge 60$).', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c1_detector', 'out_atlas_poster', 'ATLAS Detector & TileCal Instrumentation', 1, 1, 'bullets-image', '**High-Multiplicity Track Trigger & Subsystems:**
- **Inner Detector:** Pixel and Semiconductor Tracker (SCT) within a 2T solenoidal field provide precision vertex reconstruction.
- **Tile Calorimeter (TileCal):** Steel/scintillating-tile sampling calorimeter for jet energy measurement and minimum-bias trigger verification.
- **Dataset:** 151 $\\mu\\text{b}^{-1}$ minimum-bias and 8.4 $\\text{nb}^{-1}$ high-multiplicity trigger streams.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[{"id":"fig_tilecal","url":"/api/workspaces/atlas-bose-einstein-correlations/assets/fig_tilecal_module.png","caption":"Figure 1: ATLAS Tile Calorimeter barrel partitioning and readout scintillator instrumentation."}]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c1_selection', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Event & Track Selection Criteria', 1, 2, 'bullets', '- **Primary Interaction Vertex:** Reconstructed primary vertex required with $\\ge 2$ associated tracks of transverse momentum $p_{\\text{T}} > 100\\text{ MeV}$.
- **Kinematic Acceptance:** Full pseudorapidity coverage $|\\eta| < 2.5$, with track quality cuts requiring $\\ge 1$ Pixel hit and $\\ge 6$ SCT silicon hits.
- **Pileup Rejection:** Low beam-luminosity operation with average pileup $\\langle \\mu \\rangle \\le 0.005$ eliminates overlapping collision events per bunch crossing.
- **Shared-Track Cleaning:** Strict vertex association rejects secondary tracks from strange hadron decays.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c2_theory', 'out_atlas_poster', 'BEC Correlation Function Formulation', 2, 0, 'bullets', 'The two-particle correlation function is measured as the ratio of like-sign pion pairs to an uncorrelated reference sample in bins of relative momentum:

$$C_2(Q) = \\frac{N(Q)}{N_{\\text{ref}}(Q)} = C_0 \\left[1 + \\lambda \\Omega(Q, R)\\right](1 + \\delta Q)$$

- **Lorentz Invariant Relative Momentum:** $Q = \\sqrt{-(p_1 - p_2)^2} = \\sqrt{M^2_{\\pi\\pi} - 4m_\\pi^2}$, where $m_\\pi = 139.57\\text{ MeV}$.
- **Source Radii $R$ & Strength $\\lambda$:** $\\Omega(Q, R) = e^{-(QR)}$ parameterizes the exponential source distribution in four dimensions.
- **Baseline Normalization:** $C_0$ normalizes the tail ($Q > 0.8\\text{ GeV}$) while $\\delta$ models long-range phase-space correlations.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c2_fit', 'out_atlas_poster', '13 TeV Correlation Fits & Radius Extraction', 2, 1, 'bullets-image', '**Exponential Fit & Extraction of Emitter Dimensions:**
- **Double-Exponential Superiority:** Successfully fits both the sharp core and long-range non-Gaussian tails.
- **Emitter Radius:** Measured source radius $R = 1.42 \\pm 0.03\\,\\text{(stat)} \\pm 0.08\\,\\text{(syst)}\\text{ fm}$.
- **Correlation Strength:** $\\lambda = 0.68 \\pm 0.02$, demonstrating partial coherence and long-lived decay contamination.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[{"id":"fig_bec_fit","url":"/api/workspaces/atlas-bose-einstein-correlations/assets/fig_bec_correlation_fit.png","caption":"Figure 2: Two-particle correlation function $C_2(Q)$ in 13 TeV pp collisions with double-exponential fit and Data/Fit ratio."}]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c2_reference', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Reference Sample & Coulomb Corrections', 2, 2, 'bullets', '- **Opposite-Sign Pion Pairs:** Primary uncorrelated reference baseline after subtracting hadronic resonance contributions ($\\rho^0, \\omega, K^0_S$).
- **Gamow Coulomb Factor:** Relativistic Coulomb interaction correction $A_{\\text{c}}(Q) = \\frac{2\\pi \\eta_c}{e^{2\\pi \\eta_c} - 1}$ with $\\eta_c = \\alpha m_\\pi / Q$ applied to like-sign and opposite-sign pairs.
- **Mixed-Event Cross-Check:** Secondary reference constructed by pairing pions from distinct events with matching vertex positions and track multiplicities.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c3_stats', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Multiplicity Dependence & Collective Behavior', 3, 0, 'stats', '- **13 TeV** Center-of-Mass Energy | Highest pp collision energy at CERN LHC
- **R = 1.42 fm** Measured Source Radius | Exponential source parameterization
- **N_ch >= 60** High Multiplicity | Clear scaling of $R \\propto \\langle N_{\\text{ch}} \\rangle^{1/3}$
- **TileCal** Trigger & Veto | Fast minimum-bias scintillation detection', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c3_systematics', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Systematic Uncertainty Breakdown', 3, 1, 'bullets-table', 'Dominant relative systematic uncertainties on the extracted radius $R$ and strength $\\lambda$:', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[["Source of Uncertainty","$\\Delta R / R$ (%)","$\\Delta \\lambda / \\lambda$ (%)"],["Track Reconstruction Efficiency","2.1","1.8"],["Reference Sample Definition","3.4","2.9"],["Coulomb Correction Modeling","1.7","2.2"],["Resonance Decay Backgrounds","2.8","3.1"],["Fit Interval Variation ($Q_{\\text{min}}, Q_{\\text{max}}$)","1.9","2.5"],["Total Systematic Uncertainty","5.6","5.4"]],"caption":"Table 1: Systematic error components at 13 TeV","hasHeader":true}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c3_conclusion', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Conclusions & Hadronization Dynamics', 3, 2, 'bullets', '- **Hydrodynamic Scaling:** $R \\propto \\langle N_{\\text{ch}} \\rangle^{1/3}$ scaling confirms collective spatial expansion analogous to relativistic heavy-ion collisions.
- **Transverse Momentum Dependence:** Significant decrease of $R$ with increasing $k_{\\text{T}}$ reveals intense space-momentum correlations during freeze-out.
- **Model Constraints:** Sets precision constraints on PYTHIA 8 Lund string fragmentation and multi-parton interaction parameters.
- **Universal BEC Freeze-out:** Consistent with continuous source expansion prior to chemical decoupling across LHC collision energies.', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_c3_refs', 'out_atlas_poster', 'Key References', 3, 3, 'bullets', '- **ATLAS Collaboration**, Eur. Phys. J. C 82, 608 (2022).
- **G. Goldhaber et al.**, Phys. Rev. 120, 300 (1960).
- **ATLAS TileCal Group**, JINST 9, P02008 (2014).', 'single', NULL, 'valid', NULL, NULL, '{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false}', '[]', '[]', NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "Card" ("id", "outputId", "title", "column", "order", "pattern", "content", "figureLayout", "heightBudget", "validation", "generatedLatex", "slideNotes", "table", "figures", "sourceIds", "grounding") VALUES ('card_atlas_slide_1', 'out_atlas_slides', 'Physics Motivation', 1, 0, 'bullets', '- Space-time geometry of the hadronization region
