y for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789943764326},{"id":"3802651d-e0a3-4d1a-8a0f-62e1dc5a5990","ts":"12:36:31 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check failed","detail":"Error: HTTP 500: {\\"error\\":\\"AI provider circuit is open for http://127.0.0.1:8045/v1/chat/completions (recent consecutive failures); skipping\\"}","status":"error","createdAt":1789943791269},{"id":"e02297fd-f8e9-4aa2-a6c1-94dffa87930a","ts":"12:36:38 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789943798122},{"id":"1d40c801-145d-4f9d-aa01-11bcf8899810","ts":"12:36:50 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check failed","detail":"Error: HTTP 500: {\\"error\\":\\"AI provider circuit is open for http://127.0.0.1:8045/v1/chat/completions (recent consecutive failures); skipping\\"}","status":"error","createdAt":1789943810021},{"id":"37686650-4b67-4425-bedd-029434424035","ts":"12:36:59 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Attempt 1/3: Saving workspace...","status":"running","createdAt":1789943819153}],"chatMessages":[],"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"deerflowEnabled":true,"outputs":[{"id":"out_attn_poster","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"poster","templateId":"gemini","title":"Attention Is All You Need","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#4F46E5","authors":"Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Łukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin","sourceIds":[],"venue":"31st Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2017), Long Beach, CA, USA","logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_tf_c3_leaderboard","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"WMT 2014 Translation Benchmark","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Translation quality on WMT 2014 English-to-German and English-to-French:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Model","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training FLOPs"],["ByteNet","23.75","—","$1.0 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["Deep-Att + PosUnk","24.60","39.92","$1.2 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","$9.6 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["MoE (Shazeer et al.)","26.03","40.56","$2.0 \\\\times 10^{19}$"],["Transformer (Base)","27.30","38.10","$3.3 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["**Transformer (Big)**","**28.40**","**41.00**","**$2.3 \\\\times 10^{19}$**"]],"caption":"Table 2: BLEU score comparison and training FLOPs on WMT 2014 translation.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c3_legacy","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Legacy: Foundation of Modern AI","column":3,"order":2,"pattern":"references","content":"- **The Architectural Foundation:** Spawned BERT, GPT-2/3/4, Gemini, Claude, LLaMA, and Vision Transformers.\\n- **Scale Without Saturation:** Proved that constant path length enables massive scaling with predictable gains.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c2_arch","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"The Transformer Architecture","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"**Encoder-Decoder Structure:** Stack of $N=6$ identical layers ($d_{\\\\text{model}}=512, d_{ff}=2048, h=8$):\\n- **Encoder:** Multi-Head Self-Attention followed by a position-wise Feed-Forward Network.\\n- **Decoder:** Adds masked attention to prevent positions from attending to subsequent tokens.\\n- **Residual Connections:** $\\\\text{LayerNorm}(x + \\\\text{Sublayer}(x))$ around every sub-layer.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Full Transformer encoder-decoder architecture with self-attention and cross-attention sub-layers."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c2_heads","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Multi-Head Attention Visualized","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"Linear projections allow the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces:\\n$$\\\\text{MultiHead}(Q,K,V) = \\\\text{Concat}(\\\\text{head}_1, \\\\dots, \\\\text{head}_h)W^O$$\\n- Different heads track distinct linguistic structures, resolving coreference and verbal syntax simultaneously.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[{"id":"fig_attention_heads","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","caption":"Figure 2: Attention weight heatmaps across heads resolving coreference across long horizons."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c3_complexity","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Computational Complexity Analysis","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Comparing layer characteristics for sequence length $n$ and representation dimension $d$:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Layer Type","Complexity / Layer","Sequential Ops","Max Path Length"],["Self-Attention","$O(n^2 \\\\cdot d)$","$O(1)$","$O(1)$"],["Recurrent (LSTM)","$O(n \\\\cdot d^2)$","$O(n)$","$O(n)$"],["Convolutional","$O(k \\\\cdot n \\\\cdot d^2)$","$O(1)$","$O(\\\\log_k(n))$"]],"caption":"Table 1: Asymptotic complexity, sequential operations, and maximum signal path lengths.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_metrics","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Breakthrough Benchmark Performance","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"stats","content":"- **28.4 BLEU** EN-DE Benchmark | New SOTA (+2.0 over previous best)\\n- **41.0 BLEU** EN-FR Benchmark | Surpasses all single models & ensembles\\n- **3.5 Days** Training Cost | 8 × NVIDIA P100 GPUs (fraction of RNN cost)\\n- **O(1)** Path Length | Constant sequential path for signal propagation","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_attention","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Scaled Dot-Product Attention","column":1,"order":2,"pattern":"bullets","content":"An attention function maps queries $Q$, keys $K$, and values $V$ to output representations:\\n\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q,K,V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left(\\\\frac{QK^\\\\top}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}\\\\right)V$$\\n\\n- **Why Scale by $\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}$?** For large values of $d_k$, dot products grow large, pushing softmax into vanishing gradient regions. Dividing by $\\\\sqrt{d_k}$ preserves stable gradients.\\n- **Matrix Parallelism:** Evaluated on entire sequences simultaneously via optimized matrix multiplications.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_abstract","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Abstract & The Recurrent Bottleneck","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"The dominant sequence models rely on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks linking an encoder and decoder.\\n\\n- **Sequential Bottleneck:** Recurrent models (LSTM, GRU) process tokens step-by-step ($O(n)$ sequential operations), prohibiting parallelization.\\n- **Signal Loss:** Information transfer between distant tokens traverses intermediate hidden states, causing vanishing gradients.\\n- **The Transformer:** Eliminates recurrence entirely, relying exclusively on **self-attention** to compute representations in $O(1)$ path length.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_attn_paper","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"paper","templateId":"article-twocol","title":"Attention Is All You Need — Preprint","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#111827","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_attn_a1","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"Abstract","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"section","content":"The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best performing models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attention mechanism. We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer, based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely. Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to be superior in quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less time to train. Our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, improving over the existing best results, including ensembles, by over 2 BLEU. On the WMT 2014 English-to-French translation task, our model establishes a new single-model state-of-the-art BLEU score of 41.0 after training for 3.5 days on eight GPUs.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a2","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"1 Introduction","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"section","content":"Recurrent neural networks, particularly Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) and gated recurrent (GRU) neural networks, have been firmly established as state-of-the-art approaches in sequence modeling. Recurrent models inherently generate sequences along symbol positions of input and output sequences. Aligning positions to computation steps precludes parallelization within training examples, which becomes critical at longer sequence lengths.\\\\n\\\\nIn this work we propose the Transformer, a model architecture eschewing recurrence and instead relying entirely on an attention mechanism to draw global dependencies between input and output.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a3","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"2 Background & Model Architecture","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"section-figure","content":"Most competitive neural sequence transduction models have an encoder-decoder structure. The Transformer follows this overall architecture using stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both the encoder and decoder. The encoder is composed of a stack of $N = 6$ identical layers. Each layer has two sub-layers: a multi-head self-attention mechanism, and a position-wise fully connected feed-forward network. We employ residual connections around each sub-layer, followed by layer normalization.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: The Transformer model architecture."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a4","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"3 Attention Mechanism","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"section","content":"An attention function can be described as mapping a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output. We compute the matrix of outputs as:\\\\n\\\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left( \\\\frac{Q K^T}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}} \\\\right) V$$\\\\n\\\\nWe scale dot products by $1 / \\\\sqrt{d_k}$ to counteract vanishing gradients when $d_k$ is large. Multi-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions simultaneously.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a5","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"4 Why Self-Attention","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"section-table","content":"We compare self-attention layers to recurrent and convolutional layers on computational complexity and path lengths between distant positions:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Layer Type","Complexity per Layer","Sequential Ops","Max Path Length"],["Self-Attention","O(n² · d)","O(1)","O(1)"],["Recurrent","O(n · d²)","O(n)","O(n)"],["Convolutional","O(k · n · d²)","O(1)","O(log_k(n))"]],"caption":"Table 1: Maximum path lengths and complexity across layer types.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a6","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"5 Experimental Results","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"section-table","content":"On the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, the big transformer model outperforms the best previously reported models by more than 2.0 BLEU, establishing a new state-of-the-art BLEU score of 28.4.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Model","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training FLOPs"],["ByteNet","23.75","—","1.0 × 10¹⁹"],["GNMT + RL","24.60","39.92","2.3 × 10¹⁹"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","9.6 × 10¹⁸"],["Transformer (base)","27.30","38.10","3.3 × 10¹⁸"],["Transformer (big)","28.40","41.00","2.3 × 10¹⁹"]],"caption":"Table 2: Translation performance on WMT 2014 EN-DE and EN-FR.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a7","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"6 Conclusion & References","column":null,"order":6,"pattern":"references","content":"In this work, we presented the Transformer, the first sequence transduction model based entirely on attention. On both WMT 2014 English-to-German and English-to-French translation tasks, we achieved state-of-the-art results while training faster than architectures based on recurrent or convolutional layers.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_attn_slides","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"slides","templateId":"beamer-metropolis","title":"Attention Is All You Need — Presentation","isActive":true,"themeColor":"#2D3748","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_attn_s1","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Title Slide","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"title-slide","content":"Attention Is All You Need\\\\n\\\\nAshish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit\\\\nLlion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Łukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin\\\\n\\\\nGoogle Brain & Google Research\\\\nNeurIPS 2017","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Introduce the authors from Google Brain and Google Research. Mention that this work introduces the Transformer architecture.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s2","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"The Recurrent Bottleneck","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Sequential Dependency:** RNNs/LSTMs compute $h_t = f(h_{t-1}, x_t)$, requiring $O(n)$ sequential operations.\\n- **Hardware Underutilization:** Sequential dependencies prevent parallel execution across GPU/TPU accelerators.\\n- **Long-Range Signal Degradation:** Information must travel through many recurrence steps, degrading context.\\n- **Question:** Can we achieve sequence transduction without any recurrence at all?","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight that sequential processing was the fundamental barrier to scaling NLP models to massive web datasets.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s3","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Scaled Dot-Product Attention","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"two-column","content":"Attention as Information Retrieval:\\n- Query ($Q$), Key ($K$), Value ($V$)\\n\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left(\\\\frac{Q K^T}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}\\\\right) V$$\\n\\nWhy scale by $\\\\sqrt{d_k}$?\\n- For large $d_k$, dot products grow large.\\n- Softmax gradient becomes vanishingly small.\\n- Scaling stabilizes gradient flow during backpropagation.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Explain the intuitive connection between queries, keys, and values like database retrieval, and emphasize why sqrt(d_k) matters.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s4","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Multi-Head Attention","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- Rather than single attention function, project $Q, K, V$ into $h=8$ subspaces of dimension $d_k = 64$.\\n- Enables attending to different positions and different syntactic/semantic aspects simultaneously.\\n- $\\\\text{MultiHead}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{Concat}(\\\\text{head}_1, \\\\dots, \\\\text{head}_h) W^O$","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Point out that different heads specialize: some track syntax, some track pronouns, others focus on neighboring tokens.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_attention_heads","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","caption":"Figure: Multi-head attention patterns."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s5","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"The Full Architecture","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"figure-slide","content":"- Encoder: $N=6$ identical layers (Self-Attention + FFN + Residual + LayerNorm).\\n- Decoder: $N=6$ identical layers (Masked Self-Attention + Cross-Attention + FFN).\\n- Sinusoidal Positional Encodings provide sequence order awareness.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Walk through the dataflow from input tokens through encoder representations to decoder auto-regressive generation.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure: Transformer encoder-decoder model."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s6","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"WMT 2014 Benchmark Results","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Breakthrough performance on machine translation benchmarks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Emphasize that the Transformer not only achieved SOTA BLEU but also trained in a fraction of the time.","table":{"rows":[["Architecture","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training Time"],["GNMT + RL","24.60","39.92","2.3 × 10¹⁹ FLOPs"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","9.6 × 10¹⁸ FLOPs"],["Transformer (base)","27.30","38.10","12 hours (8 GPUs)"],["Transformer (big)","28.40","41.00","3.5 days (8 GPUs)"]],"caption":"Table: Machine translation benchmark comparison.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s7","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Conclusion & Legacy","column":null,"order":6,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **First entirely attention-based transduction model:** Proved recurrence is not necessary for sequence learning.\\n- **Superior parallelization:** Massive training speedups over RNNs and CNNs.\\n- **The Foundation of Frontier AI:** Directly spawned BERT, GPT-2/3/4, Claude, Gemini, Vision Transformers, and AlphaFold 2.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Close by summarizing how this single 2017 paper transformed the entire field of artificial intelligence.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]}],"assets":[{"id":"ast_tf_arch","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_transformer_arch.png","filename":"fig_transformer_arch.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Transformer Encoder-Decoder Architecture","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_tf_attn","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_attention_heads.png","filename":"fig_attention_heads.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Multi-Head Attention Weights","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_tf_bleu","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_bleu_comparison.png","filename":"fig_bleu_comparison.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_bleu_comparison.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"BLEU vs Training FLOPs","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null}],"ingestFiles":[{"id":"doc_transformer_2017","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","name":"Attention Is All You Need.pdf","size":40013,"method":"vlm","status":"done","progress":100,"error":null,"dismissed":false,"vectorChunks":100,"vectorIndexedAt":"2026-09-20T22:01:33.735Z","vectorStatus":"ready"}]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "WorkspaceSnapshot" ("id", "workspaceId", "savedAt", "label", "source", "revision", "snapshot") VALUES ('cmuaeembg002n3i14urbwk3or', 'attention-is-all-you-need', '2026-09-20T22:38:58.684Z', 'Added new card: "WMT 2014 Translation Be', 'human', 8, '{"id":"attention-is-all-you-need","name":"Attention Is All You Need","authors":"Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Łukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin","venue":"NeurIPS 2017 (Google Brain & Google Research)","userId":"user_3IGDYw03LkmHZaaCgKwWcBYxHQu","bibContent":"@inproceedings{vaswani2017attention,\\n  title={Attention Is All You Need},\\n  author={Vaswani, Ashish and Shazeer, Noam and Parmar, Niki and Uszkoreit, Jakob and Jones, Llion and Gomez, Aidan N and Kaiser, {\\\\L}ukasz and Polosukhin, Illia},\\n  booktitle={Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)},\\n  volume={30},\\n  pages={5998--6008},\\n  year={2017}\\n}","revision":8,"bibKeys":null,"agentEvents":[{"id":"init","ts":"07:45:18 PM","kind":"info","title":"Editor ready","detail":"Loading workspace…","status":"done"},{"id":"37268a38-9892-460d-a2e2-0d3402fc695b","ts":"07:45:52 PM","kind":"info","title":"Workspace loaded","detail":"7 cards · gemini","status":"done","createdAt":1789926352237},{"id":"5945d5a4-868e-4150-b563-bf5a97b44893","ts":"07:46:00 PM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789926360427},{"id":"946f2c69-87f9-41fd-b67f-8c064e8f18ad","ts":"07:46:05 PM","kind":"info","title":"Layout Inspection Passed","detail":"No visual overflows detected.","status":"done","createdAt":1789926365952},{"id":"6832a0a0-bf87-4f4f-b3b9-34018ecf3e1d","ts":"07:46:18 PM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789926378291},{"id":"f2d0b1d9-8de6-4f74-88dc-8d28a6d3a02d","ts":"07:46:29 PM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for p