":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789943764326},{"id":"3802651d-e0a3-4d1a-8a0f-62e1dc5a5990","ts":"12:36:31 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check failed","detail":"Error: HTTP 500: {\\"error\\":\\"AI provider circuit is open for http://127.0.0.1:8045/v1/chat/completions (recent consecutive failures); skipping\\"}","status":"error","createdAt":1789943791269},{"id":"e02297fd-f8e9-4aa2-a6c1-94dffa87930a","ts":"12:36:38 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789943798122},{"id":"1d40c801-145d-4f9d-aa01-11bcf8899810","ts":"12:36:50 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check failed","detail":"Error: HTTP 500: {\\"error\\":\\"AI provider circuit is open for http://127.0.0.1:8045/v1/chat/completions (recent consecutive failures); skipping\\"}","status":"error","createdAt":1789943810021},{"id":"37686650-4b67-4425-bedd-029434424035","ts":"12:36:59 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789943819153},{"id":"b9ee40ad-d8f0-4e2a-9625-c1a6f2c93a87","ts":"12:37:17 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check failed","detail":"Error: HTTP 500: {\\"error\\":\\"AI provider circuit is open for http://127.0.0.1:8045/v1/chat/completions (recent consecutive failures); skipping\\"}","status":"error","createdAt":1789943837140},{"id":"857b6df4-2ba4-45ea-a34a-2747f0771851","ts":"12:38:52 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Attempt 1/3: Saving workspace...","status":"running","createdAt":1789943932028}],"chatMessages":[],"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"deerflowEnabled":true,"outputs":[{"id":"out_attn_poster","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"poster","templateId":"gemini","title":"Attention Is All You Need","isActive":true,"themeColor":"#4F46E5","authors":"Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Łukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin","sourceIds":[],"venue":"31st Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2017), Long Beach, CA, USA","logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_tf_c3_leaderboard","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"WMT 2014 Translation Benchmark","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Translation quality on WMT 2014 English-to-German and English-to-French:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Model","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training FLOPs"],["ByteNet","23.75","—","$1.0 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["Deep-Att + PosUnk","24.60","39.92","$1.2 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","$9.6 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["MoE (Shazeer et al.)","26.03","40.56","$2.0 \\\\times 10^{19}$"],["Transformer (Base)","27.30","38.10","$3.3 \\\\times 10^{18}$"],["**Transformer (Big)**","**28.40**","**41.00**","**$2.3 \\\\times 10^{19}$**"]],"caption":"Table 2: BLEU score comparison and training FLOPs on WMT 2014 translation.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c3_legacy","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Legacy: Foundation of Modern AI","column":3,"order":2,"pattern":"references","content":"- **The Architectural Foundation:** Spawned BERT, GPT-2/3/4, Gemini, Claude, LLaMA, and Vision Transformers.\\n- **Scale Without Saturation:** Proved that constant path length enables massive scaling with predictable gains.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c2_arch","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"The Transformer Architecture","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"**Encoder-Decoder Structure:** Stack of $N=6$ identical layers ($d_{\\\\text{model}}=512, d_{ff}=2048, h=8$):\\n- **Encoder:** Multi-Head Self-Attention followed by a position-wise Feed-Forward Network.\\n- **Decoder:** Adds masked attention to prevent positions from attending to subsequent tokens.\\n- **Residual Connections:** $\\\\text{LayerNorm}(x + \\\\text{Sublayer}(x))$ around every sub-layer.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Full Transformer encoder-decoder architecture with self-attention and cross-attention sub-layers."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c2_heads","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Multi-Head Attention Visualized","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"Linear projections allow the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces:\\n$$\\\\text{MultiHead}(Q,K,V) = \\\\text{Concat}(\\\\text{head}_1, \\\\dots, \\\\text{head}_h)W^O$$\\n- Different heads track distinct linguistic structures, resolving coreference and verbal syntax simultaneously.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[{"id":"fig_attention_heads","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","caption":"Figure 2: Attention weight heatmaps across heads resolving coreference across long horizons."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c3_complexity","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Computational Complexity Analysis","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Comparing layer characteristics for sequence length $n$ and representation dimension $d$:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Layer Type","Complexity / Layer","Sequential Ops","Max Path Length"],["Self-Attention","$O(n^2 \\\\cdot d)$","$O(1)$","$O(1)$"],["Recurrent (LSTM)","$O(n \\\\cdot d^2)$","$O(n)$","$O(n)$"],["Convolutional","$O(k \\\\cdot n \\\\cdot d^2)$","$O(1)$","$O(\\\\log_k(n))$"]],"caption":"Table 1: Asymptotic complexity, sequential operations, and maximum signal path lengths.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_metrics","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Breakthrough Benchmark Performance","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"stats","content":"- **28.4 BLEU** EN-DE Benchmark | New SOTA (+2.0 over previous best)\\n- **41.0 BLEU** EN-FR Benchmark | Surpasses all single models & ensembles\\n- **3.5 Days** Training Cost | 8 × NVIDIA P100 GPUs (fraction of RNN cost)\\n- **O(1)** Path Length | Constant sequential path for signal propagation","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_attention","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Scaled Dot-Product Attention","column":1,"order":2,"pattern":"bullets","content":"An attention function maps queries $Q$, keys $K$, and values $V$ to output representations:\\n\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q,K,V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left(\\\\frac{QK^\\\\top}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}\\\\right)V$$\\n\\n- **Why Scale by $\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}$?** For large values of $d_k$, dot products grow large, pushing softmax into vanishing gradient regions. Dividing by $\\\\sqrt{d_k}$ preserves stable gradients.\\n- **Matrix Parallelism:** Evaluated on entire sequences simultaneously via optimized matrix multiplications.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_tf_c1_abstract","outputId":"out_attn_poster","title":"Abstract & The Recurrent Bottleneck","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"The dominant sequence models rely on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks linking an encoder and decoder.\\n\\n- **Sequential Bottleneck:** Recurrent models (LSTM, GRU) process tokens step-by-step ($O(n)$ sequential operations), prohibiting parallelization.\\n- **Signal Loss:** Information transfer between distant tokens traverses intermediate hidden states, causing vanishing gradients.\\n- **The Transformer:** Eliminates recurrence entirely, relying exclusively on **self-attention** to compute representations in $O(1)$ path length.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"valid","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":false},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_attn_paper","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"paper","templateId":"article-twocol","title":"Attention Is All You Need — Preprint","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#111827","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_attn_a1","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"Abstract","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"section","content":"The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best performing models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attention mechanism. We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer, based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely. Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to be superior in quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less time to train. Our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, improving over the existing best results, including ensembles, by over 2 BLEU. On the WMT 2014 English-to-French translation task, our model establishes a new single-model state-of-the-art BLEU score of 41.0 after training for 3.5 days on eight GPUs.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a2","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"1 Introduction","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"section","content":"Recurrent neural networks, particularly Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) and gated recurrent (GRU) neural networks, have been firmly established as state-of-the-art approaches in sequence modeling. Recurrent models inherently generate sequences along symbol positions of input and output sequences. Aligning positions to computation steps precludes parallelization within training examples, which becomes critical at longer sequence lengths.\\\\n\\\\nIn this work we propose the Transformer, a model architecture eschewing recurrence and instead relying entirely on an attention mechanism to draw global dependencies between input and output.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a3","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"2 Background & Model Architecture","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"section-figure","content":"Most competitive neural sequence transduction models have an encoder-decoder structure. The Transformer follows this overall architecture using stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both the encoder and decoder. The encoder is composed of a stack of $N = 6$ identical layers. Each layer has two sub-layers: a multi-head self-attention mechanism, and a position-wise fully connected feed-forward network. We employ residual connections around each sub-layer, followed by layer normalization.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: The Transformer model architecture."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a4","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"3 Attention Mechanism","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"section","content":"An attention function can be described as mapping a query and a set of key-value pairs to an output. We compute the matrix of outputs as:\\\\n\\\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left( \\\\frac{Q K^T}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}} \\\\right) V$$\\\\n\\\\nWe scale dot products by $1 / \\\\sqrt{d_k}$ to counteract vanishing gradients when $d_k$ is large. Multi-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions simultaneously.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a5","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"4 Why Self-Attention","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"section-table","content":"We compare self-attention layers to recurrent and convolutional layers on computational complexity and path lengths between distant positions:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Layer Type","Complexity per Layer","Sequential Ops","Max Path Length"],["Self-Attention","O(n² · d)","O(1)","O(1)"],["Recurrent","O(n · d²)","O(n)","O(n)"],["Convolutional","O(k · n · d²)","O(1)","O(log_k(n))"]],"caption":"Table 1: Maximum path lengths and complexity across layer types.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a6","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"5 Experimental Results","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"section-table","content":"On the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, the big transformer model outperforms the best previously reported models by more than 2.0 BLEU, establishing a new state-of-the-art BLEU score of 28.4.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Model","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training FLOPs"],["ByteNet","23.75","—","1.0 × 10¹⁹"],["GNMT + RL","24.60","39.92","2.3 × 10¹⁹"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","9.6 × 10¹⁸"],["Transformer (base)","27.30","38.10","3.3 × 10¹⁸"],["Transformer (big)","28.40","41.00","2.3 × 10¹⁹"]],"caption":"Table 2: Translation performance on WMT 2014 EN-DE and EN-FR.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_a7","outputId":"out_attn_paper","title":"6 Conclusion & References","column":null,"order":6,"pattern":"references","content":"In this work, we presented the Transformer, the first sequence transduction model based entirely on attention. On both WMT 2014 English-to-German and English-to-French translation tasks, we achieved state-of-the-art results while training faster than architectures based on recurrent or convolutional layers.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_attn_slides","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","outputType":"slides","templateId":"beamer-metropolis","title":"Attention Is All You Need — Presentation","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#2D3748","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_attn_s1","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Title Slide","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"title-slide","content":"Attention Is All You Need\\\\n\\\\nAshish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit\\\\nLlion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Łukasz Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin\\\\n\\\\nGoogle Brain & Google Research\\\\nNeurIPS 2017","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Introduce the authors from Google Brain and Google Research. Mention that this work introduces the Transformer architecture.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s2","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"The Recurrent Bottleneck","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Sequential Dependency:** RNNs/LSTMs compute $h_t = f(h_{t-1}, x_t)$, requiring $O(n)$ sequential operations.\\n- **Hardware Underutilization:** Sequential dependencies prevent parallel execution across GPU/TPU accelerators.\\n- **Long-Range Signal Degradation:** Information must travel through many recurrence steps, degrading context.\\n- **Question:** Can we achieve sequence transduction without any recurrence at all?","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight that sequential processing was the fundamental barrier to scaling NLP models to massive web datasets.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s3","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Scaled Dot-Product Attention","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"two-column","content":"Attention as Information Retrieval:\\n- Query ($Q$), Key ($K$), Value ($V$)\\n\\n$$\\\\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{softmax}\\\\left(\\\\frac{Q K^T}{\\\\sqrt{d_k}}\\\\right) V$$\\n\\nWhy scale by $\\\\sqrt{d_k}$?\\n- For large $d_k$, dot products grow large.\\n- Softmax gradient becomes vanishingly small.\\n- Scaling stabilizes gradient flow during backpropagation.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Explain the intuitive connection between queries, keys, and values like database retrieval, and emphasize why sqrt(d_k) matters.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s4","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Multi-Head Attention","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- Rather than single attention function, project $Q, K, V$ into $h=8$ subspaces of dimension $d_k = 64$.\\n- Enables attending to different positions and different syntactic/semantic aspects simultaneously.\\n- $\\\\text{MultiHead}(Q, K, V) = \\\\text{Concat}(\\\\text{head}_1, \\\\dots, \\\\text{head}_h) W^O$","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Point out that different heads specialize: some track syntax, some track pronouns, others focus on neighboring tokens.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_attention_heads","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","caption":"Figure: Multi-head attention patterns."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s5","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"The Full Architecture","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"figure-slide","content":"- Encoder: $N=6$ identical layers (Self-Attention + FFN + Residual + LayerNorm).\\n- Decoder: $N=6$ identical layers (Masked Self-Attention + Cross-Attention + FFN).\\n- Sinusoidal Positional Encodings provide sequence order awareness.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Walk through the dataflow from input tokens through encoder representations to decoder auto-regressive generation.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_transformer_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","caption":"Figure: Transformer encoder-decoder model."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s6","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"WMT 2014 Benchmark Results","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Breakthrough performance on machine translation benchmarks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Emphasize that the Transformer not only achieved SOTA BLEU but also trained in a fraction of the time.","table":{"rows":[["Architecture","EN-DE BLEU","EN-FR BLEU","Training Time"],["GNMT + RL","24.60","39.92","2.3 × 10¹⁹ FLOPs"],["ConvS2S","25.16","40.46","9.6 × 10¹⁸ FLOPs"],["Transformer (base)","27.30","38.10","12 hours (8 GPUs)"],["Transformer (big)","28.40","41.00","3.5 days (8 GPUs)"]],"caption":"Table: Machine translation benchmark comparison.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_attn_s7","outputId":"out_attn_slides","title":"Conclusion & Legacy","column":null,"order":6,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **First entirely attention-based transduction model:** Proved recurrence is not necessary for sequence learning.\\n- **Superior parallelization:** Massive training speedups over RNNs and CNNs.\\n- **The Foundation of Frontier AI:** Directly spawned BERT, GPT-2/3/4, Claude, Gemini, Vision Transformers, and AlphaFold 2.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Close by summarizing how this single 2017 paper transformed the entire field of artificial intelligence.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]}],"assets":[{"id":"ast_tf_arch","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_transformer_arch.png","filename":"fig_transformer_arch.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_transformer_arch.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Transformer Encoder-Decoder Architecture","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_tf_attn","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_attention_heads.png","filename":"fig_attention_heads.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_attention_heads.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Multi-Head Attention Weights","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_tf_bleu","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","fileId":"fig_bleu_comparison.png","filename":"fig_bleu_comparison.png","url":"/api/workspaces/attention-is-all-you-need/assets/fig_bleu_comparison.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"BLEU vs Training FLOPs","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null}],"ingestFiles":[{"id":"doc_transformer_2017","workspaceId":"attention-is-all-you-need","name":"Attention Is All You Need.pdf","size":40013,"method":"vlm","status":"done","progress":100,"error":null,"dismissed":false,"vectorChunks":100,"vectorIndexedAt":"2026-09-20T22:01:33.735Z","vectorStatus":"ready"}]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "WorkspaceSnapshot" ("id", "workspaceId", "savedAt", "label", "source", "revision", "snapshot") VALUES ('cmuaftaa100023irkl8idcjrn', 'deerflow-super-agent', '2026-09-20T23:18:22.537Z', 'Created initial project layout', 'human', 1, '{"id":"deerflow-super-agent","name":"DeerFlow 2.0: Open-Source Super Agent Harness","authors":"DeerFlow Core Team, ByteDance Open Source, and Community Contributors","venue":"Open Source AI & Agentic Systems Symposium 2026 (GitHub #1 Trending)","userId":"user_3IGDYw03LkmHZaaCgKwWcBYxHQu","bibContent":"@article{deerflow2026harness,\\n  title={DeerFlow 2.0: An Open-Source Super Agent Harness Orchestrating Sandboxed Execution, Memory, and Extensible Skills},\\n  author={DeerFlow Core Team and Contributors},\\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2602.14699},\\n  year={2026}\\n}","revision":1,"bibKeys":null,"agentEvents":[{"id":"init","ts":"01:18:08 AM","kind":"info","title":"Editor ready","detail":"Loading workspace…","status":"done"},{"id":"878be9e7-11cd-49a4-83eb-61649de29c05","ts":"01:18:09 AM","kind":"info","title":"Workspace loaded","detail":"7 cards · conference","status":"done","createdAt":1789946289300},{"id":"dd0a2064-bb8f-4f82-8168-26d8089dfe63","ts":"01:18:11 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946291908},{"id":"016800ea-9fc4-4740-bca4-d0c86e0e7dbe","ts":"01:18:18 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946298986},{"id":"23bc6093-43ee-425f-ae15-2847a66d7d9e","ts":"01:18:19 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Attempt 1/3: Saving workspace...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946299250}],"chatMessages":[],"logoUrl":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/deer_logo.png","secondaryLogoUrl":null,"deerflowEnabled":true,"outputs":[{"id":"out_df_poster_conf","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"conference","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Harness — Conference Poster","isActive":true,"themeColor":"#0284C7","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p1_abs","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Abstract & Motivation","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Beyond Brittle Chatbots:** Modern AI agents must transition from simple single-turn dialog to resilient, multi-step problem solving with persistent state.\\n- **Core Engineering Challenge:** Autonomous execution requires tight sandboxing, non-leaking context engineering, multi-turn long-term memory, and parallel sub-agent delegation.\\n- **DeerFlow 2.0:** A ground-up rewrite providing an extensible super-agent harness powered by LangGraph, Docker/K8s micro-sandboxes, and dynamic SKILL.md protocols.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_stats","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"System Milestones & Benchmarks","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"stats","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending** Global Open-Source Launch (Feb 2026)\\n- **78.4% Pass@1** Multi-Step Real-World Engineering Benchmark\\n- **O(1) Memory Lookup** Hierarchical Vector & Key-Value Retrieval Store\\n- **<50ms Isolation** Sandboxed Container Spawn & Execution Latency","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"End-to-End System Topology","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- **Unified Gateway (Port 8001):** FastAPI REST API with embedded LangGraph-compatible runtime and multi-mode SSE delta streaming.\\n- **Lead Agent Orchestration:** Bounded middleware chain enforcing AuthZ, context window compaction, dynamic planning, and tool sandboxing.\\n- **Multi-Channel Ingress:** Bridges seamlessly across Next.js Web UI, Slack, Feishu, Discord, Telegram, and CLI terminal.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Full DeerFlow 2.0 multi-agent harness architecture."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_subagents","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Subagent Delegation & Parallelization","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Deterministic Execution Split:** Server-side execution ID handles process registry, while client tool-call ID maintains transparent UI message tuples.\\n- **Specialized Sidecars:** Lead agent dispatches ephemeral background workers for CPU-heavy code execution, literature crawl, and test verification.\\n- **Terminal Token Accounting:** Subagent consumption is precisely tracked in parent run metadata, preventing unbounded context expansion.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_eval","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Empirical Performance & Ablation","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"Comparative evaluation across autonomous research and programming challenges against leading open-source agent frameworks:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_bench","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","caption":"Figure 2: Benchmark comparison on complex multi-step tasks."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Component Evaluation Matrix","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"table","content":"Ablation analysis on multi-step reasoning accuracy and token efficiency:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Architecture Setup","Success Rate","Token Budget","Execution Safety"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.0x (Baseline)","Unprotected"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.4x","Host Privileges"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.1x","Limited Docker"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Super-Agent)","78.4% SOTA","1.7x (Compacted)","Zero-Trust K8s/Docker"]],"caption":"Table 1: Benchmark pass rates and token savings.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Conclusion & Future Work","column":3,"order":2,"pattern":"references","content":"- **Production Ready:** Fully isolated micro-containers guarantee safe shell execution on enterprise infrastructures.\\n- **Ecosystem:** Active integrations with BytePlus InfoQuest, Langfuse, OpenTelemetry, and Model Context Protocol (MCP).\\n- **Open-Source:** Code, schemas, and extension harnesses freely available on GitHub under MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_poster_gemini","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"gemini","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Deep Research & Sandbox Harness — Gemini Poster","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#4F46E5","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p2_intro","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Introduction & System Principles","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **DeerFlow Philosophy:** Deep Exploration and Efficient Research Flow with true per-thread isolation.\\n- **Stateful Persistence:** SQLite/Postgres checkpointing preserves exact tool call graph and rollback points.\\n- **Model Agnostic:** First-class compatibility with Doubao-Seed-2.0, DeepSeek v3, Kimi 2.5, Claude 3.7, and GPT-4o.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_sandbox","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Secure Micro-Sandbox Architecture","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Containerized Isolation:** Read-only root filesystem with ephemeral memory tmpfs.\\n- **Atomic Tool Primitives:** File tools ensure exact diff streaming to the browser.\\n- **Network Containment:** Egress filtering blocks unauthorized metadata service and intranet queries.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Harness Topology Overview","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- Multi-tiered Gateway orchestrating subgraphs, long-running MCP workers, and dynamic skills.\\n- Leased scheduler prevents task overlap in multi-instance deployments.\\n- Real-time SSE streaming with bounded token batching.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch2","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Micro-service architecture of DeerFlow 2.0."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_memory","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Long-Term Memory & Reflection","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Automated Reflection:** Post-turn background observers extract enduring facts, user preferences, and project rules.\\n- **Dynamic Context Compaction:** Automatically truncates stale tool call logs while preserving core goals.\\n- **Hybrid Retrieval:** Dense embeddings paired with keyword BM25 for accurate multi-turn recall.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Benchmark Results & Throughput","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"System performance under sustained concurrent research tasks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Metric / Component","Direct Docker","K8s Provisioner","Speedup"],["Sandbox Init Latency","120 ms","45 ms","2.6x"],["Tool Delta Streaming","12 ms batch","8 ms batch","1.5x"],["Peak Concurrent Threads","64 threads","512 threads","8.0x"],["Memory Footprint / Turn","24 MB","18 MB","-25%"]],"caption":"Table 1: System latency and throughput metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Summary & Open-Source Ecosystem","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"references","content":"- **ByteDance Volcengine Coding Plan:** Backed by state-of-the-art enterprise frontier models.\\n- **Sister Project LLM Space:** Companion developer workbench for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- Available at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow under the MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_paper","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"paper","templateId":"neurips","title":"DeerFlow: An Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness for Sandboxed Exploration and Verified Code Synthesis","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#111827","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_a1_abs","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"Abstract","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"section","content":"Autonomous language model agents must reliably execute arbitrary software tools, navigate expansive code repositories, synthesize verified solutions, and maintain state over extended operational horizons. We introduce DeerFlow 2.0, an open-source super-agent harness built atop a LangGraph foundation that couples sandboxed execution, hierarchical memory, subagent delegation, and extensible skill protocols. Unlike fragile single-loop architectures, DeerFlow isolates untrusted execution environments within micro-containers, enforces bounded context compaction, and orchestrates delegated subagents with independent namespaces and deterministic lifecycle accounting. On real-world multi-step engineering and research benchmarks, DeerFlow achieves a 78.4% success rate while reducing redundant context tokens by 45% compared to monolithic agent loops.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a2_intro","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"1 Introduction","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"section","content":"The evolution of foundation models has enabled agentic workflows capable of writing code, performing web research, and operating external computational tools. However, deploying agents in production environments exposes severe structural vulnerabilities: unbounded execution risks, context window exhaustion, cascading hallucination loops, and lack of persistent memory across sessions.\\\\n\\\\nTo resolve these challenges, DeerFlow 2.0 provides a modular super-agent harness designed for enterprise-grade safety and efficiency. We decouple the lead agent''s reasoning loop from tool execution through a pluggable sandbox layer supporting local container engines and Kubernetes provisioners. Furthermore, we establish a formal delegation contract where subagents inherit execution namespaces without contaminating the parent run state.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a3_arch","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"2 System Architecture & Harness Pipeline","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"section-figure","content":"The DeerFlow system topology comprises four coordinated layers: (i) an Nginx reverse-proxy ingress managing persistent Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming connections; (ii) a FastAPI Gateway hosting the embedded LangGraph runtime, authentication, and session routers; (iii) the LangGraph Lead Agent orchestrating a bounded middleware chain including dynamic authorization, session goals, and manual context compaction; and (iv) an isolated Sandbox Provisioner executing shell commands, file modifications, and web crawlers.\\\\n\\\\nSubagent delegation is decoupled through a two-tier identifier mechanism: server-side execution keys manage process lifecycles and cancellation fencing, while client tool IDs maintain transparent streaming message tuples.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_paper","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology and isolated multi-agent orchestration."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a4_eval","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"3 Experimental Evaluation","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"section-table","content":"We benchmark DeerFlow against baseline agent architectures on multi-step software engineering and complex reasoning tasks. All models were evaluated under identical budget constraints using DeepSeek v3 and Doubao-Seed-2.0 backends.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Framework Architecture","Success Rate (%)","Token Cost Ratio","Mean Latency (s)"],["Direct Zero-Shot Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","4.2s"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.40x","38.5s"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.10x","65.2s"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Full Harness)","78.4%","1.70x","24.8s"]],"caption":"Table 1: Task resolution success rate and efficiency metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a5_concl","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"4 Conclusion & Availability","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"references","content":"DeerFlow 2.0 demonstrates that orchestrating sandboxed micro-containers, stateful long-term memory, and modular subagents yields superior task completion and execution safety compared to traditional monolithic agent loops. DeerFlow is fully open-source under the MIT license and actively maintained by the open-source AI community.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_slides","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"slides","templateId":"beamer-metropolis","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Super Agent Harness — Conference Presentation","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#2D3748","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_s5_bench","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Empirical Results: SWE-Bench & GAIA","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Significant gains across autonomous engineering benchmarks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the 78.4% pass rate and emphasize the token economy achieved through smart context compaction.","table":{"rows":[["System Architecture","Pass@1 Rate","Token Economy","Safety Guarantee"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","None"],["Standard ReAct Agent","44.2%","2.40x","Host Risk"],["DeerFlow 1.x","58.6%","3.10x","Partial"],["DeerFlow 2.0 Super-Agent","78.4% SOTA","1.70x","Full Containerization"]],"caption":"Table: Benchmark accuracy and token efficiency.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s6_summary","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Summary & Community Impact","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending:** Embraced globally with rapid open-source community adoption.\\n- **Production Ready:** Pre-built Helm charts, Docker Compose, and multi-instance scheduler leases.\\n- **Companion Tooling:** LLM Space for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- **Try It Today:** Open source at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow (MIT License).","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Conclude with the link to the official repository and the invitation to contribute.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s1_title","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Title Slide","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"title-slide","content":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness\\\\n\\\\nOrchestrating Sub-Agents, Sandboxes, Memory, and Extensible Skills\\\\n\\\\nByteDance Open Source & Community Contributors\\\\nOpen Source AI Symposium 2026","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Introduce DeerFlow as the #1 trending open-source super-agent framework that transitioned from pure deep research to a universal harness.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s2_limits","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"The Limits of Monolithic LLM Agents","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Vulnerability:** Unsandboxed shell execution risks host filesystem corruption and credentials leakage.\\n- **Context Exhaustion:** Large multi-turn tool traces trigger quadratic attention costs and prompt degradation.\\n- **Fragile State:** Stateless REST wrappers lose context upon network drops or server restarts.\\n- **Need:** A durable, containerized, multi-agent harness with deterministic thread isolation.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the core engineering pain points that motivated the complete rewrite from v1 to v2.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s3_core","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Four Pillars of DeerFlow 2.0","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"two-column","content":"1. Sandboxed Micro-Containers:\\n- Ephemeral Docker / K8s runtimes\\n- Non-root, read-only rootfs\\n- Real-time diff delta streaming\\n\\n2. Hierarchical Memory Engine:\\n- User & project profiles\\n- Automatic post-run reflection\\n\\n3. Delegated Subagents:\\n- Ephemeral workers with isolated scopes\\n\\n4. Extensible SKILL.md & MCP:\\n- Dynamic plugin discovery at runtime","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Walk through the four pillars clearly explaining how they combine to form a super agent.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s4_arch","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"System Topology & Execution Pipeline","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"figure-slide","content":"- Reverse-proxy Nginx (Port 2026) handles SSE compression bypass and multi-channel ingress.\\n- FastAPI Gateway (Port 8001) embeds the LangGraph runtime with atomic transaction locks.\\n- Sandboxes execute tools in isolated environments with resource constraints.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Describe the separation of concerns between Nginx ingress, Gateway REST API, and Sandbox worker provisioner.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_slide","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]}],"assets":[{"id":"ast_df_logo","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"deer_logo.png","filename":"deer_logo.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/deer_logo.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"DeerFlow Logo","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_df_arch","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","filename":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"DeerFlow 2.0 System Architecture & Pipeline","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_df_bench","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","filename":"fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Deep Research Task Performance Comparison","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null}],"ingestFiles":[]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "WorkspaceSnapshot" ("id", "workspaceId", "savedAt", "label", "source", "revision", "snapshot") VALUES ('cmuaftxt800053irkl27xmsol', 'deerflow-super-agent', '2026-09-20T23:18:53.037Z', NULL, 'human', 2, '{"id":"deerflow-super-agent","name":"DeerFlow 2.0: Open-Source Super Agent Harness","authors":"DeerFlow Core Team, ByteDance Open Source, and Community Contributors","venue":"Open Source AI & Agentic Systems Symposium 2026 (GitHub #1 Trending)","userId":"user_3IGDYw03LkmHZaaCgKwWcBYxHQu","bibContent":"@article{deerflow2026harness,\\n  title={DeerFlow 2.0: An Open-Source Super Agent Harness Orchestrating Sandboxed Execution, Memory, and Extensible Skills},\\n  author={DeerFlow Core Team and Contributors},\\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2602.14699},\\n  year={2026}\\n}","revision":2,"bibKeys":null,"agentEvents":[{"id":"init","ts":"01:18:08 AM","kind":"info","title":"Editor ready","detail":"Loading workspace…","status":"done"},{"id":"878be9e7-11cd-49a4-83eb-61649de29c05","ts":"01:18:09 AM","kind":"info","title":"Workspace loaded","detail":"7 cards · conference","status":"done","createdAt":1789946289300},{"id":"dd0a2064-bb8f-4f82-8168-26d8089dfe63","ts":"01:18:11 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946291908},{"id":"016800ea-9fc4-4740-bca4-d0c86e0e7dbe","ts":"01:18:18 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946298986},{"id":"23bc6093-43ee-425f-ae15-2847a66d7d9e","ts":"01:18:19 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946299250},{"id":"e1b04af4-b600-4080-93a0-b229a67c77b1","ts":"01:18:29 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946309487},{"id":"a89e2f0f-99a7-4608-8aac-65aa1047749e","ts":"01:18:50 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Attempt 1/3: Saving workspace...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946330490}],"chatMessages":[],"logoUrl":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/deer_logo.png","secondaryLogoUrl":null,"deerflowEnabled":true,"outputs":[{"id":"out_df_poster_conf","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"conference","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Harness — Conference Poster","isActive":true,"themeColor":"#059669","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p1_abs","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Abstract & Motivation","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Beyond Brittle Chatbots:** Modern AI agents must transition from simple single-turn dialog to resilient, multi-step problem solving with persistent state.\\n- **Core Engineering Challenge:** Autonomous execution requires tight sandboxing, non-leaking context engineering, multi-turn long-term memory, and parallel sub-agent delegation.\\n- **DeerFlow 2.0:** A ground-up rewrite providing an extensible super-agent harness powered by LangGraph, Docker/K8s micro-sandboxes, and dynamic SKILL.md protocols.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"End-to-End System Topology","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- **Unified Gateway (Port 8001):** FastAPI REST API with embedded LangGraph-compatible runtime and multi-mode SSE delta streaming.\\n- **Lead Agent Orchestration:** Bounded middleware chain enforcing AuthZ, context window compaction, dynamic planning, and tool sandboxing.\\n- **Multi-Channel Ingress:** Bridges seamlessly across Next.js Web UI, Slack, Feishu, Discord, Telegram, and CLI terminal.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Full DeerFlow 2.0 multi-agent harness architecture."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_subagents","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Subagent Delegation & Parallelization","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Deterministic Execution Split:** Server-side execution ID handles process registry, while client tool-call ID maintains transparent UI message tuples.\\n- **Specialized Sidecars:** Lead agent dispatches ephemeral background workers for CPU-heavy code execution, literature crawl, and test verification.\\n- **Terminal Token Accounting:** Subagent consumption is precisely tracked in parent run metadata, preventing unbounded context expansion.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_eval","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Empirical Performance & Ablation","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"Comparative evaluation across autonomous research and programming challenges against leading open-source agent frameworks:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_bench","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","caption":"Figure 2: Benchmark comparison on complex multi-step tasks."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Component Evaluation Matrix","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"table","content":"Ablation analysis on multi-step reasoning accuracy and token efficiency:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Architecture Setup","Success Rate","Token Budget","Execution Safety"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.0x (Baseline)","Unprotected"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.4x","Host Privileges"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.1x","Limited Docker"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Super-Agent)","78.4% SOTA","1.7x (Compacted)","Zero-Trust K8s/Docker"]],"caption":"Table 1: Benchmark pass rates and token savings.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Conclusion & Future Work","column":3,"order":2,"pattern":"references","content":"- **Production Ready:** Fully isolated micro-containers guarantee safe shell execution on enterprise infrastructures.\\n- **Ecosystem:** Active integrations with BytePlus InfoQuest, Langfuse, OpenTelemetry, and Model Context Protocol (MCP).\\n- **Open-Source:** Code, schemas, and extension harnesses freely available on GitHub under MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_stats","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"System Milestones & Benchmarks","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"stats","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending** Global Open-Source Launch (Feb 2026)\\n- **78.4% Pass@1** Multi-Step Real-World Engineering Benchmark\\n- **O(1) Memory Lookup** Hierarchical Vector & Key-Value Retrieval Store\\n- **<50ms Isolation** Sandboxed Container Spawn & Execution Latency","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_poster_gemini","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"gemini","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Deep Research & Sandbox Harness — Gemini Poster","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#4F46E5","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p2_intro","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Introduction & System Principles","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **DeerFlow Philosophy:** Deep Exploration and Efficient Research Flow with true per-thread isolation.\\n- **Stateful Persistence:** SQLite/Postgres checkpointing preserves exact tool call graph and rollback points.\\n- **Model Agnostic:** First-class compatibility with Doubao-Seed-2.0, DeepSeek v3, Kimi 2.5, Claude 3.7, and GPT-4o.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_sandbox","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Secure Micro-Sandbox Architecture","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Containerized Isolation:** Read-only root filesystem with ephemeral memory tmpfs.\\n- **Atomic Tool Primitives:** File tools ensure exact diff streaming to the browser.\\n- **Network Containment:** Egress filtering blocks unauthorized metadata service and intranet queries.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Harness Topology Overview","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- Multi-tiered Gateway orchestrating subgraphs, long-running MCP workers, and dynamic skills.\\n- Leased scheduler prevents task overlap in multi-instance deployments.\\n- Real-time SSE streaming with bounded token batching.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch2","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Micro-service architecture of DeerFlow 2.0."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_memory","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Long-Term Memory & Reflection","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Automated Reflection:** Post-turn background observers extract enduring facts, user preferences, and project rules.\\n- **Dynamic Context Compaction:** Automatically truncates stale tool call logs while preserving core goals.\\n- **Hybrid Retrieval:** Dense embeddings paired with keyword BM25 for accurate multi-turn recall.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Benchmark Results & Throughput","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"System performance under sustained concurrent research tasks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Metric / Component","Direct Docker","K8s Provisioner","Speedup"],["Sandbox Init Latency","120 ms","45 ms","2.6x"],["Tool Delta Streaming","12 ms batch","8 ms batch","1.5x"],["Peak Concurrent Threads","64 threads","512 threads","8.0x"],["Memory Footprint / Turn","24 MB","18 MB","-25%"]],"caption":"Table 1: System latency and throughput metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Summary & Open-Source Ecosystem","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"references","content":"- **ByteDance Volcengine Coding Plan:** Backed by state-of-the-art enterprise frontier models.\\n- **Sister Project LLM Space:** Companion developer workbench for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- Available at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow under the MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_paper","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"paper","templateId":"neurips","title":"DeerFlow: An Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness for Sandboxed Exploration and Verified Code Synthesis","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#111827","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_a2_intro","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"1 Introduction","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"section","content":"The evolution of foundation models has enabled agentic workflows capable of writing code, performing web research, and operating external computational tools. However, deploying agents in production environments exposes severe structural vulnerabilities: unbounded execution risks, context window exhaustion, cascading hallucination loops, and lack of persistent memory across sessions.\\\\n\\\\nTo resolve these challenges, DeerFlow 2.0 provides a modular super-agent harness designed for enterprise-grade safety and efficiency. We decouple the lead agent''s reasoning loop from tool execution through a pluggable sandbox layer supporting local container engines and Kubernetes provisioners. Furthermore, we establish a formal delegation contract where subagents inherit execution namespaces without contaminating the parent run state.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a3_arch","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"2 System Architecture & Harness Pipeline","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"section-figure","content":"The DeerFlow system topology comprises four coordinated layers: (i) an Nginx reverse-proxy ingress managing persistent Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming connections; (ii) a FastAPI Gateway hosting the embedded LangGraph runtime, authentication, and session routers; (iii) the LangGraph Lead Agent orchestrating a bounded middleware chain including dynamic authorization, session goals, and manual context compaction; and (iv) an isolated Sandbox Provisioner executing shell commands, file modifications, and web crawlers.\\\\n\\\\nSubagent delegation is decoupled through a two-tier identifier mechanism: server-side execution keys manage process lifecycles and cancellation fencing, while client tool IDs maintain transparent streaming message tuples.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_paper","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology and isolated multi-agent orchestration."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a4_eval","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"3 Experimental Evaluation","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"section-table","content":"We benchmark DeerFlow against baseline agent architectures on multi-step software engineering and complex reasoning tasks. All models were evaluated under identical budget constraints using DeepSeek v3 and Doubao-Seed-2.0 backends.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Framework Architecture","Success Rate (%)","Token Cost Ratio","Mean Latency (s)"],["Direct Zero-Shot Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","4.2s"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.40x","38.5s"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.10x","65.2s"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Full Harness)","78.4%","1.70x","24.8s"]],"caption":"Table 1: Task resolution success rate and efficiency metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a5_concl","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"4 Conclusion & Availability","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"references","content":"DeerFlow 2.0 demonstrates that orchestrating sandboxed micro-containers, stateful long-term memory, and modular subagents yields superior task completion and execution safety compared to traditional monolithic agent loops. DeerFlow is fully open-source under the MIT license and actively maintained by the open-source AI community.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a1_abs","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"Abstract","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"section","content":"Autonomous language model agents must reliably execute arbitrary software tools, navigate expansive code repositories, synthesize verified solutions, and maintain state over extended operational horizons. We introduce DeerFlow 2.0, an open-source super-agent harness built atop a LangGraph foundation that couples sandboxed execution, hierarchical memory, subagent delegation, and extensible skill protocols. Unlike fragile single-loop architectures, DeerFlow isolates untrusted execution environments within micro-containers, enforces bounded context compaction, and orchestrates delegated subagents with independent namespaces and deterministic lifecycle accounting. On real-world multi-step engineering and research benchmarks, DeerFlow achieves a 78.4% success rate while reducing redundant context tokens by 45% compared to monolithic agent loops.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_slides","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"slides","templateId":"beamer-metropolis","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Super Agent Harness — Conference Presentation","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#2D3748","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_s1_title","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Title Slide","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"title-slide","content":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness\\\\n\\\\nOrchestrating Sub-Agents, Sandboxes, Memory, and Extensible Skills\\\\n\\\\nByteDance Open Source & Community Contributors\\\\nOpen Source AI Symposium 2026","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Introduce DeerFlow as the #1 trending open-source super-agent framework that transitioned from pure deep research to a universal harness.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s2_limits","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"The Limits of Monolithic LLM Agents","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Vulnerability:** Unsandboxed shell execution risks host filesystem corruption and credentials leakage.\\n- **Context Exhaustion:** Large multi-turn tool traces trigger quadratic attention costs and prompt degradation.\\n- **Fragile State:** Stateless REST wrappers lose context upon network drops or server restarts.\\n- **Need:** A durable, containerized, multi-agent harness with deterministic thread isolation.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the core engineering pain points that motivated the complete rewrite from v1 to v2.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s3_core","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Four Pillars of DeerFlow 2.0","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"two-column","content":"1. Sandboxed Micro-Containers:\\n- Ephemeral Docker / K8s runtimes\\n- Non-root, read-only rootfs\\n- Real-time diff delta streaming\\n\\n2. Hierarchical Memory Engine:\\n- User & project profiles\\n- Automatic post-run reflection\\n\\n3. Delegated Subagents:\\n- Ephemeral workers with isolated scopes\\n\\n4. Extensible SKILL.md & MCP:\\n- Dynamic plugin discovery at runtime","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Walk through the four pillars clearly explaining how they combine to form a super agent.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s4_arch","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"System Topology & Execution Pipeline","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"figure-slide","content":"- Reverse-proxy Nginx (Port 2026) handles SSE compression bypass and multi-channel ingress.\\n- FastAPI Gateway (Port 8001) embeds the LangGraph runtime with atomic transaction locks.\\n- Sandboxes execute tools in isolated environments with resource constraints.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Describe the separation of concerns between Nginx ingress, Gateway REST API, and Sandbox worker provisioner.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_slide","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s5_bench","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Empirical Results: SWE-Bench & GAIA","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Significant gains across autonomous engineering benchmarks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the 78.4% pass rate and emphasize the token economy achieved through smart context compaction.","table":{"rows":[["System Architecture","Pass@1 Rate","Token Economy","Safety Guarantee"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","None"],["Standard ReAct Agent","44.2%","2.40x","Host Risk"],["DeerFlow 1.x","58.6%","3.10x","Partial"],["DeerFlow 2.0 Super-Agent","78.4% SOTA","1.70x","Full Containerization"]],"caption":"Table: Benchmark accuracy and token efficiency.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s6_summary","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Summary & Community Impact","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending:** Embraced globally with rapid open-source community adoption.\\n- **Production Ready:** Pre-built Helm charts, Docker Compose, and multi-instance scheduler leases.\\n- **Companion Tooling:** LLM Space for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- **Try It Today:** Open source at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow (MIT License).","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Conclude with the link to the official repository and the invitation to contribute.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]}],"assets":[{"id":"ast_df_logo","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"deer_logo.png","filename":"deer_logo.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/deer_logo.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"DeerFlow Logo","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_df_arch","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","filename":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"DeerFlow 2.0 System Architecture & Pipeline","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null},{"id":"ast_df_bench","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","filename":"fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","kind":"figure","page":1,"section":null,"bbox":null,"confidence":"high","heading":null,"snippet":null,"thumbnailUrl":null,"caption":"Deep Research Task Performance Comparison","assignedCardId":null,"assignedSlot":null,"tableRows":null}],"ingestFiles":[]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO "WorkspaceSnapshot" ("id", "workspaceId", "savedAt", "label", "source", "revision", "snapshot") VALUES ('cmuag3es500083irkdtgxqj83', 'deerflow-super-agent', '2026-09-20T23:26:14.933Z', 'Restructured document cards', 'human', 3, '{"id":"deerflow-super-agent","name":"DeerFlow 2.0: Open-Source Super Agent Harness","authors":"DeerFlow Core Team, ByteDance Open Source, and Community Contributors","venue":"Open Source AI & Agentic Systems Symposium 2026 (GitHub #1 Trending)","userId":"user_3IGDYw03LkmHZaaCgKwWcBYxHQu","bibContent":"@article{deerflow2026harness,\\n  title={DeerFlow 2.0: An Open-Source Super Agent Harness Orchestrating Sandboxed Execution, Memory, and Extensible Skills},\\n  author={DeerFlow Core Team and Contributors},\\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2602.14699},\\n  year={2026}\\n}","revision":3,"bibKeys":null,"agentEvents":[{"id":"init","ts":"01:18:08 AM","kind":"info","title":"Editor ready","detail":"Loading workspace…","status":"done"},{"id":"878be9e7-11cd-49a4-83eb-61649de29c05","ts":"01:18:09 AM","kind":"info","title":"Workspace loaded","detail":"7 cards · conference","status":"done","createdAt":1789946289300},{"id":"dd0a2064-bb8f-4f82-8168-26d8089dfe63","ts":"01:18:11 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946291908},{"id":"016800ea-9fc4-4740-bca4-d0c86e0e7dbe","ts":"01:18:18 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","detail":"Interrupted","status":"error","createdAt":1789946298986},{"id":"23bc6093-43ee-425f-ae15-2847a66d7d9e","ts":"01:18:19 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"PDF ready for preview.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946299250},{"id":"e1b04af4-b600-4080-93a0-b229a67c77b1","ts":"01:18:29 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","detail":"Interrupted","status":"error","createdAt":1789946309487},{"id":"a89e2f0f-99a7-4608-8aac-65aa1047749e","ts":"01:18:50 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Interrupted","status":"error","createdAt":1789946330490},{"id":"9f0709fb-179a-455b-bc0d-6a8f29c2ef6b","ts":"01:26:06 AM","kind":"info","title":"Workspace loaded","detail":"7 cards · conference","status":"done","createdAt":1789946766275},{"id":"be1aff0b-4200-4760-91d0-9b5c5d2653e5","ts":"01:26:08 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compile succeeded","detail":"Cached preview ready.","status":"done","createdAt":1789946768850},{"id":"3e1770ff-6f23-40de-8ff3-62aef9b963b1","ts":"01:26:09 AM","kind":"info","title":"VLM Layout Check running...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946769795},{"id":"81b25a2c-c45d-4052-b984-dfd4a873e60e","ts":"01:26:11 AM","kind":"generate","title":"Compiling poster with pdflatex…","detail":"Attempt 1/3: Saving workspace...","status":"running","createdAt":1789946771787}],"chatMessages":[],"logoUrl":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/deer_logo.png","secondaryLogoUrl":null,"deerflowEnabled":true,"outputs":[{"id":"out_df_poster_gemini","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"gemini","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Deep Research & Sandbox Harness — Gemini Poster","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#4F46E5","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p2_intro","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Introduction & System Principles","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **DeerFlow Philosophy:** Deep Exploration and Efficient Research Flow with true per-thread isolation.\\n- **Stateful Persistence:** SQLite/Postgres checkpointing preserves exact tool call graph and rollback points.\\n- **Model Agnostic:** First-class compatibility with Doubao-Seed-2.0, DeepSeek v3, Kimi 2.5, Claude 3.7, and GPT-4o.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_sandbox","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Secure Micro-Sandbox Architecture","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Containerized Isolation:** Read-only root filesystem with ephemeral memory tmpfs.\\n- **Atomic Tool Primitives:** File tools ensure exact diff streaming to the browser.\\n- **Network Containment:** Egress filtering blocks unauthorized metadata service and intranet queries.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Harness Topology Overview","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- Multi-tiered Gateway orchestrating subgraphs, long-running MCP workers, and dynamic skills.\\n- Leased scheduler prevents task overlap in multi-instance deployments.\\n- Real-time SSE streaming with bounded token batching.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch2","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Micro-service architecture of DeerFlow 2.0."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_memory","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Long-Term Memory & Reflection","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Automated Reflection:** Post-turn background observers extract enduring facts, user preferences, and project rules.\\n- **Dynamic Context Compaction:** Automatically truncates stale tool call logs while preserving core goals.\\n- **Hybrid Retrieval:** Dense embeddings paired with keyword BM25 for accurate multi-turn recall.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Benchmark Results & Throughput","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"System performance under sustained concurrent research tasks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Metric / Component","Direct Docker","K8s Provisioner","Speedup"],["Sandbox Init Latency","120 ms","45 ms","2.6x"],["Tool Delta Streaming","12 ms batch","8 ms batch","1.5x"],["Peak Concurrent Threads","64 threads","512 threads","8.0x"],["Memory Footprint / Turn","24 MB","18 MB","-25%"]],"caption":"Table 1: System latency and throughput metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p2_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_gemini","title":"Summary & Open-Source Ecosystem","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"references","content":"- **ByteDance Volcengine Coding Plan:** Backed by state-of-the-art enterprise frontier models.\\n- **Sister Project LLM Space:** Companion developer workbench for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- Available at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow under the MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_paper","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"paper","templateId":"neurips","title":"DeerFlow: An Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness for Sandboxed Exploration and Verified Code Synthesis","isActive":true,"themeColor":"#111827","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_a5_concl","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"4 Conclusion & Availability","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"references","content":"DeerFlow 2.0 demonstrates that orchestrating sandboxed micro-containers, stateful long-term memory, and modular subagents yields superior task completion and execution safety compared to traditional monolithic agent loops. DeerFlow is fully open-source under the MIT license and actively maintained by the open-source AI community.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a2_intro","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"1 Introduction","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"section","content":"The evolution of foundation models has enabled agentic workflows capable of writing code, performing web research, and operating external computational tools. However, deploying agents in production environments exposes severe structural vulnerabilities: unbounded execution risks, context window exhaustion, cascading hallucination loops, and lack of persistent memory across sessions.\\\\n\\\\nTo resolve these challenges, DeerFlow 2.0 provides a modular super-agent harness designed for enterprise-grade safety and efficiency. We decouple the lead agent''s reasoning loop from tool execution through a pluggable sandbox layer supporting local container engines and Kubernetes provisioners. Furthermore, we establish a formal delegation contract where subagents inherit execution namespaces without contaminating the parent run state.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a3_arch","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"2 System Architecture & Harness Pipeline","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"section-figure","content":"The DeerFlow system topology comprises four coordinated layers: (i) an Nginx reverse-proxy ingress managing persistent Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming connections; (ii) a FastAPI Gateway hosting the embedded LangGraph runtime, authentication, and session routers; (iii) the LangGraph Lead Agent orchestrating a bounded middleware chain including dynamic authorization, session goals, and manual context compaction; and (iv) an isolated Sandbox Provisioner executing shell commands, file modifications, and web crawlers.\\\\n\\\\nSubagent delegation is decoupled through a two-tier identifier mechanism: server-side execution keys manage process lifecycles and cancellation fencing, while client tool IDs maintain transparent streaming message tuples.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_paper","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology and isolated multi-agent orchestration."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a4_eval","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"3 Experimental Evaluation","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"section-table","content":"We benchmark DeerFlow against baseline agent architectures on multi-step software engineering and complex reasoning tasks. All models were evaluated under identical budget constraints using DeepSeek v3 and Doubao-Seed-2.0 backends.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Framework Architecture","Success Rate (%)","Token Cost Ratio","Mean Latency (s)"],["Direct Zero-Shot Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","4.2s"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.40x","38.5s"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.10x","65.2s"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Full Harness)","78.4%","1.70x","24.8s"]],"caption":"Table 1: Task resolution success rate and efficiency metrics.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_a1_abs","outputId":"out_df_paper","title":"Abstract","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"section","content":"Autonomous language model agents must reliably execute arbitrary software tools, navigate expansive code repositories, synthesize verified solutions, and maintain state over extended operational horizons. We introduce DeerFlow 2.0, an open-source super-agent harness built atop a LangGraph foundation that couples sandboxed execution, hierarchical memory, subagent delegation, and extensible skill protocols. Unlike fragile single-loop architectures, DeerFlow isolates untrusted execution environments within micro-containers, enforces bounded context compaction, and orchestrates delegated subagents with independent namespaces and deterministic lifecycle accounting. On real-world multi-step engineering and research benchmarks, DeerFlow achieves a 78.4% success rate while reducing redundant context tokens by 45% compared to monolithic agent loops.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_slides","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"slides","templateId":"beamer-metropolis","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Super Agent Harness — Conference Presentation","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#2D3748","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_s5_bench","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Empirical Results: SWE-Bench & GAIA","column":null,"order":4,"pattern":"bullets-table","content":"Significant gains across autonomous engineering benchmarks:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the 78.4% pass rate and emphasize the token economy achieved through smart context compaction.","table":{"rows":[["System Architecture","Pass@1 Rate","Token Economy","Safety Guarantee"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.00x","None"],["Standard ReAct Agent","44.2%","2.40x","Host Risk"],["DeerFlow 1.x","58.6%","3.10x","Partial"],["DeerFlow 2.0 Super-Agent","78.4% SOTA","1.70x","Full Containerization"]],"caption":"Table: Benchmark accuracy and token efficiency.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s6_summary","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Summary & Community Impact","column":null,"order":5,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending:** Embraced globally with rapid open-source community adoption.\\n- **Production Ready:** Pre-built Helm charts, Docker Compose, and multi-instance scheduler leases.\\n- **Companion Tooling:** LLM Space for step-by-step agent replay and failure diagnosis.\\n- **Try It Today:** Open source at github.com/bytedance/deer-flow (MIT License).","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Conclude with the link to the official repository and the invitation to contribute.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s1_title","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Title Slide","column":null,"order":0,"pattern":"title-slide","content":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Super Harness\\\\n\\\\nOrchestrating Sub-Agents, Sandboxes, Memory, and Extensible Skills\\\\n\\\\nByteDance Open Source & Community Contributors\\\\nOpen Source AI Symposium 2026","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Introduce DeerFlow as the #1 trending open-source super-agent framework that transitioned from pure deep research to a universal harness.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s2_limits","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"The Limits of Monolithic LLM Agents","column":null,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Vulnerability:** Unsandboxed shell execution risks host filesystem corruption and credentials leakage.\\n- **Context Exhaustion:** Large multi-turn tool traces trigger quadratic attention costs and prompt degradation.\\n- **Fragile State:** Stateless REST wrappers lose context upon network drops or server restarts.\\n- **Need:** A durable, containerized, multi-agent harness with deterministic thread isolation.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Highlight the core engineering pain points that motivated the complete rewrite from v1 to v2.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s3_core","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"Four Pillars of DeerFlow 2.0","column":null,"order":2,"pattern":"two-column","content":"1. Sandboxed Micro-Containers:\\n- Ephemeral Docker / K8s runtimes\\n- Non-root, read-only rootfs\\n- Real-time diff delta streaming\\n\\n2. Hierarchical Memory Engine:\\n- User & project profiles\\n- Automatic post-run reflection\\n\\n3. Delegated Subagents:\\n- Ephemeral workers with isolated scopes\\n\\n4. Extensible SKILL.md & MCP:\\n- Dynamic plugin discovery at runtime","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Walk through the four pillars clearly explaining how they combine to form a super agent.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_s4_arch","outputId":"out_df_slides","title":"System Topology & Execution Pipeline","column":null,"order":3,"pattern":"figure-slide","content":"- Reverse-proxy Nginx (Port 2026) handles SSE compression bypass and multi-channel ingress.\\n- FastAPI Gateway (Port 8001) embeds the LangGraph runtime with atomic transaction locks.\\n- Sandboxes execute tools in isolated environments with resource constraints.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":"Describe the separation of concerns between Nginx ingress, Gateway REST API, and Sandbox worker provisioner.","table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch_slide","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure: DeerFlow 2.0 system topology."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]},{"id":"out_df_poster_conf","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","outputType":"poster","templateId":"conference","title":"DeerFlow 2.0: Autonomous Multi-Agent Harness — Conference Poster","isActive":false,"themeColor":"#059669","authors":null,"sourceIds":[],"venue":null,"logoUrl":null,"secondaryLogoUrl":null,"cards":[{"id":"card_df_p1_abs","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Abstract & Motivation","column":1,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Beyond Brittle Chatbots:** Modern AI agents must transition from simple single-turn dialog to resilient, multi-step problem solving with persistent state.\\n- **Core Engineering Challenge:** Autonomous execution requires tight sandboxing, non-leaking context engineering, multi-turn long-term memory, and parallel sub-agent delegation.\\n- **DeerFlow 2.0:** A ground-up rewrite providing an extensible super-agent harness powered by LangGraph, Docker/K8s micro-sandboxes, and dynamic SKILL.md protocols.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_arch","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"End-to-End System Topology","column":2,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"- **Unified Gateway (Port 8001):** FastAPI REST API with embedded LangGraph-compatible runtime and multi-mode SSE delta streaming.\\n- **Lead Agent Orchestration:** Bounded middleware chain enforcing AuthZ, context window compaction, dynamic planning, and tool sandboxing.\\n- **Multi-Channel Ingress:** Bridges seamlessly across Next.js Web UI, Slack, Feishu, Discord, Telegram, and CLI terminal.","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_arch","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_arch.png","caption":"Figure 1: Full DeerFlow 2.0 multi-agent harness architecture."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_subagents","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Subagent Delegation & Parallelization","column":2,"order":1,"pattern":"bullets","content":"- **Deterministic Execution Split:** Server-side execution ID handles process registry, while client tool-call ID maintains transparent UI message tuples.\\n- **Specialized Sidecars:** Lead agent dispatches ephemeral background workers for CPU-heavy code execution, literature crawl, and test verification.\\n- **Terminal Token Accounting:** Subagent consumption is precisely tracked in parent run metadata, preventing unbounded context expansion.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_eval","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Empirical Performance & Ablation","column":3,"order":0,"pattern":"bullets-image","content":"Comparative evaluation across autonomous research and programming challenges against leading open-source agent frameworks:","figureLayout":"single","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[{"id":"fig_df_bench","url":"/api/workspaces/deerflow-super-agent/assets/fig_deerflow_benchmark.png","caption":"Figure 2: Benchmark comparison on complex multi-step tasks."}],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_table","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Component Evaluation Matrix","column":3,"order":1,"pattern":"table","content":"Ablation analysis on multi-step reasoning accuracy and token efficiency:","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[["Architecture Setup","Success Rate","Token Budget","Execution Safety"],["Direct LLM Prompting","28.5%","1.0x (Baseline)","Unprotected"],["Single-Thread ReAct","44.2%","2.4x","Host Privileges"],["DeerFlow 1.x (Research Only)","58.6%","3.1x","Limited Docker"],["DeerFlow 2.0 (Super-Agent)","78.4% SOTA","1.7x (Compacted)","Zero-Trust K8s/Docker"]],"caption":"Table 1: Benchmark pass rates and token savings.","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_concl","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"Conclusion & Future Work","column":3,"order":2,"pattern":"references","content":"- **Production Ready:** Fully isolated micro-containers guarantee safe shell execution on enterprise infrastructures.\\n- **Ecosystem:** Active integrations with BytePlus InfoQuest, Langfuse, OpenTelemetry, and Model Context Protocol (MCP).\\n- **Open-Source:** Code, schemas, and extension harnesses freely available on GitHub under MIT license.","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null},{"id":"card_df_p1_stats","outputId":"out_df_poster_conf","title":"System Milestones & Benchmarks","column":1,"order":1,"pattern":"stats","content":"- **#1 GitHub Trending** Global Open-Source Launch (Feb 2026)\\n- **78.4% Pass@1** Multi-Step Real-World Engineering Benchmark\\n- **O(1) Memory Lookup** Hierarchical Vector & Key-Value Retrieval Store\\n- **<50ms Isolation** Sandboxed Container Spawn & Execution Latency","figureLayout":"auto","heightBudget":null,"validation":"ok","generatedLatex":null,"slideNotes":null,"table":{"rows":[],"caption":"","hasHeader":true},"figures":[],"sourceIds":[],"grounding":null}]}],"assets":[{"id":"ast_df_arch","workspaceId":"deerflow-super-agent","fileId":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","filename":"fig_deerflow_arch.png","url":